# Changelog Before Commit

Before creating any git commit, verify `CHANGELOG.md` has an entry that matches the change being committed.

- If `CHANGELOG.md` is missing a relevant note, add one before committing.
- If the commit is intentionally non-user-facing, explicitly confirm with the user that skipping changelog is acceptable.
- During pre-commit checks, always review staged/unstaged changes and confirm changelog coverage.
